  "document": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Responsive images | Example Notes</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Responsive images: a short essay used as a test page.\">\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Ines Varga\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Responsive images\">\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-06-01T08:00:00Z\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<header><nav><a href=\"/\">Home</a> <a href=\"/about\">About</a></nav></header>\n<article>\n<h1>Responsive images</h1>\n<p class=\"byline\">By Ines Varga</p>\n<p>The committee met in the old library on the hill, where the winter light fell across the long oak tables, and the members argued, as they always did, about the cost of repairing the roof.</p>\n<p>Nobody could remember who had first proposed the plan, but by the second hour it had acquired the weight of tradition, and dissent, when it came, was polite and brief.</p>\n<p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p>\n<p>Outside, the river rose slowly against the stone bridge, carrying branches and the first ice of the year, and a boy on the far bank counted the pieces as they passed under the arch.</p><p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p><picture><source srcset=\"/a-800.webp 800w, /a-400.webp 400w\" type=\"image/webp\"><source srcset=\"/a.jpg\" media=\"(min-width:600px)\"><img src=\"/a-fallback.jpg\" alt=\"Six\"></picture><p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p><picture><source media=\"(min-width: 800px)\" srcset=\"/wide.jpg 800w\"><source media=\"(min-width: 400px)\" srcset=\"/mid.jpg 1600w 2x\"><img alt=\"Seven\"></picture><p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p><picture><source srcset=\"/only.webp 1x, /only2.webp 2x\"></picture><p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://cdn.test/image/fetch/$s_!Yb!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fx.test%2Fa.png 424w, https://cdn.test/image/fetch/$s_!Yb!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fx.test%2Fa.png 848w\"><img src=\"https://cdn.test/a.png\" alt=\"Eight\"></picture><p>Nobody could remember who had first proposed the plan, but by the second hour it had acquired the weight of tradition, and dissent, when it came, was polite and brief.</p>\n<p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p>\n<p>Outside, the river rose slowly against the stone bridge, carrying branches and the first ice of the year, and a boy on the far bank counted the pieces as they passed under the arch.</p>\n<p>The committee met in the old library on the hill, where the winter light fell across the long oak tables, and the members argued, as they always did, about the cost of repairing the roof.</p>\n</article>\n<footer><p>Copyright Example Notes</p></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
